<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Joe_Shuster> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Joseph Shuster (/ˈʃuːstər/; July 10, 1914 – July 30, 1992) was a Canadian-American comic book artist best known for co-creating the DC Comics character Superman, with Jerry Siegel, in Action Comics #1 (cover-dated June 1938). Shuster was involved in a number of legal battles over ownership of the Superman character. His comic book career after Superman was relatively unsuccessful, and by the mid-1970s, Shuster had left the field completely due to partial blindness."@en .
