<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lightning_(DC_Comics)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Lightning** is a fictional [superhero](:Superhero) appearing in [American comic books](:American_comic_books) published by [DC Comics](:DC_Comics). Not pinpointed with direct reference, Lightning first appears in the miniseries *[Kingdom Come](:Kingdom_Come_%28comics%29)* in 1996, written by [Mark Waid](:Mark_Waid) and illustrated by [Alex Ross](:Alex_Ross). The character is given official introduction in *Justice Society of America* vol. 3 #12 (March 2008), written by [Geoff Johns](:Geoff_Johns) and illustrated by [Dale Eaglesham](:Dale_Eaglesham) in the [Modern Age of Comic Books](:Modern_Age_of_Comic_Books).Born **Jennifer Pierce**, she was born a [metahuman](:Metahuman) in the [DC Universe](:DC_Universe). She is the second child of superhero [Black Lightning](:Black_Lightning) and the younger sibling of Anissa Pierce, the heroine known as [Thunder](:Thunder_%28comics%29). Forbidden to use their abilities until completing their educations, Pierce was put in contact and later becomes a member of the superhero team the [Justice Society of America](:Justice_Society_of_America). Her father orchestrates this so Jennifer would not endure the hardships her sister did while transitioning into crimefighting. She possesses abilities similar to her father's of electrical generation and manipulation as well as flight. Thus far in her narrative, Pierce has not gained full control of her abilities.Along with comic books, Lightning has made appearances in various television shows and the character was portrayed by [China Anne McClain](:China_Anne_McClain) in the live action [Arrowverse](:Arrowverse) series *[Black Lightning](:Black_Lightning_%28TV_series%29)*, and with Laura Kariuki taking over the role in the remaining episodes of the [final season](:Black_Lightning_%28season_4%29). McClain returned in the final episode of the show."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
