<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sal_Trapani> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Salvatore A. \"Sal\" Trapani** (April 30, 1927—July 14, 1999) was an American [comic-book](:Comic-book) artist active from the 1940s [Golden Age of comics](:Golden_Age_of_comics) through the 1960s [Silver Age](:Silver_Age_of_comics) and into the 1980s. He is best known as a journeyman [inker](:Inker) and occasional [penciller](:Penciller) for a variety of comics publishers."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
