<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Frank_McLaughlin_(artist)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Francis X. McLaughlin** (March 18, 1935 – March 4, 2020) was an [American](:Americans) [comics artist](:Comics_artist) who co-created the [comic book](:Comic_book) character [Judomaster](:Judomaster), drew the [comic strip](:Comic_strip) *[Gil Thorp](:Gil_Thorp)*, and assisted on such strips as *[Brenda Starr, Reporter](:Brenda_Starr%2C_Reporter)* and *[The Heart of Juliet Jones](:The_Heart_of_Juliet_Jones)*. He also wrote and illustrated books about [cartooning](:Cartooning) and comic art."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
