<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spirit_King> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Spirit King** is a character in the fictional [DC Universe](:DC_Universe); he was initially an adversary of the original [Mister Terrific](:Mister_Terrific_%28Terry_Sloane%29), but later expanded to be a threat to the entire [Justice Society](:Justice_Society), particularly the [Spectre](:Spectre_%28comics%29) and the [Flash](:Jay_Garrick).The character was created for a murder mystery story in the 1970s and retroactively introduced into the fictional history of the character [Mister Terrific](:Mister_Terrific_%28comics%29)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bill_Everett> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/wikiPageRevisionID> "1121031686"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bryan_Hitch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Bryan Hitch** (born 22 April 1970) is a British [comics artist](:Comics_artist) and  [writer](:Comic_book_writer). Hitch began his career in the United Kingdom for [Marvel UK](:Marvel_UK), working on titles such as *[Action Force](:Action_Force)* and *[Death's Head](:Death%27s_Head)*, before gaining prominence on American titles such as [Wildstorm](:Wildstorm)'s *[Stormwatch](:Stormwatch_%28comics%29)* and *[The Authority](:The_Authority_%28comics%29)*, [DC Comics](:DC_Comics)' *[JLA](:JLA_%28comic_book%29)*, and [Marvel Comics](:Marvel_Comics)' *[The Ultimates](:The_Ultimates)*.Hitch's artwork and designs have appeared in [direct-to-video](:Direct-to-video) animated films, television, and major [feature films](:Feature_films), such as the 2009 film *[Star Trek](:Star_Trek_%28film%29)*, for which he has been praised by director [J. J. Abrams](:J%2E_J%2E_Abrams)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Rulah,_Jungle_Goddess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Rulah, Jungle Goddess** is a [fictional character](:Fictional_character), a [jungle girl](:Jungle_girl), in [comic books](:Comic_books) published by [Fox Feature Syndicate](:Fox_Feature_Syndicate). She first appeared in *Zoot Comics* #7 (June 1947). [Matt Baker](:Matt_Baker_%28artist%29) designed her, before [Jack Kamen](:Jack_Kamen) and [Graham Ingels](:Graham_Ingels) helped develop her image.Rulah was inspired by a boom in jungle girl comics in the late 1940s, headed by Fiction House's [Sheena, Queen of the Jungle](:Sheena%2C_Queen_of_the_Jungle)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Centrix> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Centrix is a fictional superhero in the DC universe and a member of the superhero team the Global Guardians."@en .
