<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ned_Leeds> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "As the Hobgoblin:**Edward** \"**Ned**\" **Leeds** is a [fictional](:Fiction) [character](:Character_%28arts%29) appearing in [American comic books](:American_comic_book) published by [Marvel Comics](:Marvel_Comics). A [supporting character](:Supporting_character) in stories featuring the superhero [Spider-Man](:Spider-Man), he has been a reporter for the *[Daily Bugle](:Daily_Bugle)*, and the [abusive husband](:Abusive_power_and_control) of [Betty Brant](:Betty_Brant). Leeds is the first character to take on the [**Hobgoblin**](:Hobgoblin_%28comics%29) mantle as a [supervillain](:Supervillain); ten years following his [assassination](:Assassination), he is [retroactively established](:Retroactive_continuity) to have been willingly [brainwashed](:Brainwashing) to serve as a [stand-in](:Stand-in) for [Roderick Kingsley](:Roderick_Kingsley) and his brother Daniel Kingsley, the true first Hobgoblins and [masterminds](https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mastermind), and killed before he could give them up to the authorities for a lesser sentence, and as such the third Hobgoblin: prior to this, from [1987](:1987_in_comics) to [1997](:1997_in_comics), Ned was originally depicted as having been the true identity of the first Hobgoblin. The character was revived in a [2018](:2018_in_comics)–[2021](:2021_in_comics) storyline where he was revealed to have been a willing Hobgoblin, faking his death to seek revenge on [the Foreigner](:Foreigner_%28character%29) for having attempted to kill him, and using the brainwashing story to convince Betty to take him back and [impregnate](:Pregnancy) her, with the character confirmed to have been the first (willing, non-brainwashed) Hobgoblin in a [2022](:2022_in_comics) storyline.[Jacob Batalon](:Jacob_Batalon) portrays [Ned Leeds](:Ned_Leeds_%28Marvel_Cinematic_Universe%29) in the [Marvel Cinematic Universe](:Marvel_Cinematic_Universe) (MCU), appearing in *[Spider-Man: Homecoming](:Spider-Man%3A_Homecoming)* (2017), *[Avengers: Infinity War](:Avengers%3A_Infinity_War)* (2018), *[Avengers: Endgame](:Avengers%3A_Endgame)* and *[Spider-Man: Far From Home](:Spider-Man%3A_Far_From_Home)* (both 2019), and *[The Daily Bugle](:The_Daily_Bugle_%28web_series%29)* and *[Spider-Man: No Way Home](:Spider-Man%3A_No_Way_Home)* (both 2021)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
