<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dennis_O'Neil> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Dennis Joseph O'Neil** (May 3, 1939 – June 11, 2020) was an American [comic book](:Comic_book) writer and editor, principally for [Marvel Comics](:Marvel_Comics) and [DC Comics](:DC_Comics) from the 1960s through the 1990s, and Group Editor for the [Batman](:Batman) family of titles until his retirement.His best-known works include *[Green Lantern/Green Arrow](:Green_Lantern/Green_Arrow)* and *Batman* with [Neal Adams](:Neal_Adams). It was during this run that O'Neil co-created the Batman villains [Ra's al Ghul](:Ra%27s_al_Ghul) and [Talia al Ghul](:Talia_al_Ghul). His other notable work includes runs on *[The Shadow](:The_Shadow)* with [Michael Kaluta](:Michael_Kaluta) and *[The Question](:Question_%28comics%29)* with [Denys Cowan](:Denys_Cowan). As an editor, he is principally known for editing the various Batman titles. He also sat on the board of directors of the charity [The Hero Initiative](:The_Hero_Initiative) and served on its Disbursement Committee."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
