<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Necrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Necrom is a fictional comic book supervillain appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics, as an enemy of the British superhero group Excalibur. Created by writer/artist Alan Davis, the character first appeared in Excalibur #46 (January, 1992), which depicted him as a powerful sorcerer who sought the power of the cosmic entity known as the Phoenix Force, with which he threatened the entire multiverse."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Operator_No._5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#Agent> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Daken> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Daken** (; birth name: **Akihiro**) is a fictional character appearing in [American comic books](:American_comic_book) published by [Marvel Comics](:Marvel_Comics). Daken was created by writer [Daniel Way](:Daniel_Way) and artist [Steve Dillon](:Steve_Dillon) and first appeared in *[Wolverine: Origins](:Wolverine%3A_Origins)* #10 (March 2007).Daken is the [mutant](:Mutant_%28Marvel_Comics%29) son of [Wolverine](:Wolverine_%28character%29) and his deceased wife [Itsu](:Daken%23Introduction_and_meeting_his_father%3A_Wolverine%3A_Origins_%282007-2009%29), possessing superhuman abilities similar to his father (e.g., healing factor, retractable claws) as well as [pheromone](:Pheromone) manipulating powers. Blaming his father for his supposed abandonment, his mother's death and traumatic childhood, Daken sought revenge against Wolverine. Daken was a member of the [Dark Avengers](:Dark_Avengers) under his father's moniker **Wolverine**, the [Brotherhood of Mutants](:Brotherhood_of_Mutants) and at one point was a **[Horseman of Death](:Horsemen_of_Apocalypse)**. After years as a [supervillain](:Supervillain) and sometime [antihero](:Antihero), Daken later reforms himself as a [superhero](:Superhero) after [relocating to Krakoa](:Dawn_of_X), reconciling with his father and becoming a member of [X-Factor](:X-Factor_%28comics%29) and the [Marauders](:Marauders_%28comic_book)#Volume_2), eventually earning the title of **[Fang](:Fang_%28comics%29)** for his heroism.Daken was ranked sixth in Comics Alliance's \"50 Sexiest Male Characters in Comics\" list and is often recognized for his [sex appeal](:Sex_appeal)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
