<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sheldon_Mayer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Sheldon Mayer (/ˈmaɪ.ər/; April 1, 1917 – December 21, 1991) was an American comics artist, writer, and editor. One of the earliest employees of Major Malcolm Wheeler-Nicholson's National Allied Publications, Mayer produced almost all of his comics work for the company that would become known as DC Comics. He is among those credited with rescuing the unsold Superman comic strip from the rejection pile."@en .
