<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Otto_Binder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Otto Oscar Binder** (; August 26, 1911 – October 13, 1974) was an American author of [science fiction](:Science_fiction) and [non-fiction](:Non-fiction) books and stories, and [comic books](:Comic_book). He is best known as the co-creator of [Supergirl](:Supergirl) and for his many scripts for *[Captain Marvel Adventures](:Captain_Marvel_%28DC_Comics)#Fawcett_years:_The_Marvel_Family,_allies,_and_enemies)* and other stories involving the entire [superhero](:Superhero) [Marvel Family](:Marvel_Family). He was prolific in the comic book field and is credited with writing over 4,400 stories across a variety of publishers under his own name, as well as more than 160 stories under the pen-name [Eando Binder](:Eando_Binder)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mangog> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mangog"@en .
