<http://dbpedia.org/resource/E._Nelson_Bridwell> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Edward Nelson Bridwell (September 22, 1931 – January 23, 1987) was a writer for Mad magazine (writing the now-famous catchphrase, \"What you mean...we?\" in a 1958 parody of The Lone Ranger in Mad) and various comic books published by DC Comics. One of the writers for the Batman comic strip and Super Friends, he also wrote The Inferior Five, among other comics. He has been called \"DC's self-appointed continuity cop.\""@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kenneth_Irons> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Kenneth Irons"@en .
