<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Warren_Ellis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Warren Girard Ellis** (born 16 February 1968) is a British comic book writer, novelist, and screenwriter. He is best known as the co-creator of several original comics series, including *[Transmetropolitan](:Transmetropolitan)* (1997–2002), *[Global Frequency](:Global_Frequency)* (2002–2004) and *[Red](:Red_%28WildStorm%29)* (2003–2004), which was adapted into the feature films *[Red](:Red_%282010_film%29)* (2010) and *[Red 2](:Red_2_%28film%29)* (2013). Ellis is the author of the novels *[Crooked Little Vein](:Crooked_Little_Vein)* (2007) and *[Gun Machine](:Gun_Machine)* (2013) and the novella *Normal* (2016).A prolific comic book writer, Ellis has written several [Marvel](:Marvel_Comics) series, including *[Astonishing X-Men](:Astonishing_X-Men)*, *[Thunderbolts](:Thunderbolts_%28comics%29)*, *[Moon Knight](:Moon_Knight)* and the \"[Extremis](:Extremis)\" story arc of *[Iron Man](:Iron_Man)*, which was the basis for the [Marvel Cinematic Universe](:Marvel_Cinematic_Universe) film *[Iron Man 3](:Iron_Man_3)* (2013). Ellis created *[The Authority](:The_Authority_%28comics%29)* and *[Planetary](:Planetary_%28comics%29)* for [WildStorm](:WildStorm), and wrote a run of *[Hellblazer](:Hellblazer)* for [Vertigo](:Vertigo_%28DC_Comics%29) and *[James Bond](:James_Bond_%28Dynamite_Entertainment%29)* for [Dynamite Entertainment](:Dynamite_Entertainment). Ellis wrote the video games [*Hostile Waters*](:Hostile_Waters%3A_Antaeus_Rising) (2001), *[Cold Winter](:Cold_Winter)* (2005), and *[Dead Space](:Dead_Space_%282008_video_game%29)* (2008). He also wrote the animated TV movie *[G.I. Joe: Resolute](:G%2EI%2E_Joe%3A_Resolute)* (2009) and served as the head writer on the acclaimed animated [Netflix](:Netflix) series *[Castlevania](:Castlevania_%28TV_series%29)* (2017–2021).Ellis is well known for [sociocultural](:Sociocultural) commentary, both through his online presence and through his writing, which covers [transhumanist](:Transhumanism) (most notably [nanotechnology](:Nanotechnology), [cryonics](:Cryonics), [mind transfer](:Mind_transfer) and [human enhancement](:Human_enhancement%29) and [folkloric](:Folklore) themes, often in combination with each other. He is a humanist and former patron of [Humanists UK](:Humanists_UK), a charity focused on promoting [humanism](:Secular_humanism) and advancing [secularism](:Secularism). He is a resident of [Southend-on-Sea](:Southend-on-Sea), England."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
