<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Superman> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Strength, Stamina, Endurance, Speed, Agility, Reflexes, Intelligence, Longevity, HearingEM Spectrum Vision, Infra-red Vision, Microscopic Vision, Telescopic Vision, X-ray Vision**Superman** is a [superhero](:Superhero) who appears in [American comic books](:American_comic_books) published by [DC Comics](:DC_Comics). The character was created by writer [Jerry Siegel](:Jerry_Siegel) and artist [Joe Shuster](:Joe_Shuster), and debuted in the comic book *[Action Comics](:Action_Comics)* [#1](:Action_Comics_1) ([cover-dated](:Cover-date) June 1938 and published April 18, 1938). Superman has been adapted to a number of other media, which includes radio serials, novels, films, television shows, theater, and video games.Superman was born on the fictional planet [Krypton](:Krypton_%28comics%29) and was named **Kal-El**. As a baby, his parents sent him to Earth in a small spaceship moments before Krypton was destroyed in a natural cataclysm. His ship landed in the American countryside, near the fictional town of [Smallville](:Smallville_%28comics%29). He was found and adopted by farmers [Jonathan and Martha Kent](:Jonathan_and_Martha_Kent), who named him **Clark Kent**. Clark developed various superhuman abilities, such as incredible strength and impervious skin. His adoptive parents advised him to use his abilities for the benefit of humanity, and he decided to fight crime. To protect his personal life, he changes into a colorful costume and uses the alias \"Superman\" when fighting crime. Clark resides in the fictional American city of [Metropolis](:Metropolis_%28comics%29), where he works as a journalist for the *[Daily Planet](:Daily_Planet)*. Superman's [supporting characters](:List_of_Superman_supporting_characters) include his [love interest](:Superman_and_Lois_Lane) and fellow journalist [Lois Lane](:Lois_Lane), *Daily Planet* photographer [Jimmy Olsen](:Jimmy_Olsen) and editor-in-chief [Perry White](:Perry_White), and [enemies](:List_of_Superman_enemies) such as [Brainiac](:Brainiac_%28character%29), [Darkseid](:Darkseid), [General Zod](:General_Zod), and his archenemy [Lex Luthor](:Lex_Luthor).Superman is the archetype of the superhero: he wears an outlandish costume, uses a codename, and fights evil with the aid of extraordinary abilities. Although there are earlier characters who arguably fit this definition, it was Superman who popularized the superhero genre and established its conventions. He was the best-selling superhero in American comic books up until the 1980s."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
