<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mort_Weisinger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Mortimer Weisinger** (; April 25, 1915 – May 7, 1978) was an American magazine and comic book editor best known for editing [DC Comics](:DC_Comics)' *[Superman](:Superman)* during the mid-1950s to 1960s, in the [Silver Age of comic books](:Silver_Age_of_comic_books). He also co-created such features as [Aquaman](:Aquaman), [Green Arrow](:Green_Arrow), [Johnny Quick](:Johnny_Quick), and [the original Vigilante](:Vigilante_%28Greg_Saunders%29), served as story editor for the *[Adventures of Superman](:Adventures_of_Superman_%28TV_series%29)* television series, and compiled the often-revised paperback *1001 Valuable Things You Can Get Free*."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
