<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Judd_Winick> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Judd Winick** (born February 12, 1970) is an American [cartoonist](:Cartoonist), [comic book writer](:Comic_book_writer) and [screenwriter](:Screenwriter), as well as a former [reality television](:Reality_television) personality. He first gained fame for his stint on [MTV](:MTV)'s *[The Real World: San Francisco](:The_Real_World%3A_San_Francisco)* in 1994, before finding success as a comic book creator with *[Pedro and Me](:Pedro_and_Me)*, an [autobiographical](:Autobiographical) [graphic novel](:Graphic_novel) about his friendship with *The Real World* castmate and [AIDS](:AIDS) educator [Pedro Zamora](:Pedro_Zamora). Winick wrote lengthy runs on [DC Comics](:DC_Comics)' *[Green Lantern](:Green_Lantern_%28comic_book%29)* and *[Green Arrow](:Green_Arrow)* series and created *[The Life and Times of Juniper Lee](:The_Life_and_Times_of_Juniper_Lee)* animated TV series for [Cartoon Network](:Cartoon_Network), which ran for three seasons.As part of his run on *[Batman](:Batman_%28comic_book%29)*, Winick wrote the 2005 storyline \"[Under the Hood](:Batman%3A_Under_the_Hood)\", which featured the return of [Jason Todd](:Jason_Todd), the second [Robin](:Robin_%28character%29) (who was murdered by the [Joker](:Joker_%28comics%29) in the 1988 storyline \"[A Death in the Family](:Batman%3A_A_Death_in_the_Family)\"), now operating as the [anti-hero](:Anti-hero) [Red Hood](:Red_Hood). Winick also wrote the prequel mini-series *[Red Hood: The Lost Days](:Red_Hood%3A_The_Lost_Days)*, which detailed the exact nature of Todd's resurrection, as well as the animated film *[Batman: Under the Red Hood](:Batman%3A_Under_the_Red_Hood)*, which adapted his original story to screen."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
