<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Joe_Madureira> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Joe Madureira** (born December 1974), often called **Joe Mad**, is an American [comic book artist](:Comic_book_artist) and game developer, best known for his work on *[Darksiders](:Darksiders)*, [Marvel Comics](:Marvel_Comics)' *[Uncanny X-Men](:Uncanny_X-Men)* and his [creator-owned](:Creator_ownership) comic book *[Battle Chasers](:Battle_Chasers)*. He is the founder of video game development companies [Vigil Games](:Vigil_Games) and [Airship Syndicate](:Airship_Syndicate).Madureira's style combines Western comic book influences (most notably the influence of artist [Arthur Adams](:Arthur_Adams_%28comics%29)) though it evolved to incorporate heavy influences from [Japanese](:Japan) [manga](:Manga) and video games."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
