<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Scribbly_the_Boy_Cartoonist> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Scribbly the Boy Cartoonist** is a comic book character created in 1936 by [Sheldon Mayer](:Sheldon_Mayer), first appearing in [Dell Comics](:Dell_Comics) and then moving to [All-American Publications](:All-American_Publications). Scribbly Jibbet is a semi-autobiographical character, presenting the adventures of a young man starting out in the cartooning business, and working for the *Morning Dispatch* newspaper. His stories were told around the [Golden Age era](:Golden_Age_of_Comics), when [American Comic Books](:American_Comic_Books) were primarily [anthologies](:Anthologies) telling more than one story in a magazine issue. Scribbly first appeared in the *Popular Comics* series, and then appeared in *[All-American Comics](:All-American_Comics)* from 1939 to 1944. He was then revived in his own series, *Scribbly*, from 1948 to 1952.All-American was one of the two companies that merged to form [DC Comics](:DC_Comics) in the 1940s, and, like all of DC's [Golden Age](:Golden_Age_of_Comic_Books) characters, Scribbly was later considered part of the \"[Earth-Two](:Earth-Two)\" continuity. In 2015, Scribbly was briefly revived in DC Comics continuity by [Paul Levitz](:Paul_Levitz), in the miniseries *[Convergence: World's Finest Comics](:Convergence_%28comics%29)*."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
