<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Rob_Liefeld> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Robert Liefeld (/ˈlaɪfəld/; born October 3, 1967) is an American comic book creator. A prominent writer and artist in the 1990s, he is known for co-creating the character Cable with writer Louise Simonson and the character Deadpool with writer Fabian Nicieza. In the early 1990s, Liefeld gained popularity due to his work on Marvel Comics' The New Mutants and later X-Force. In 1992, he and several other popular Marvel illustrators left the company to found Image Comics, which started a wave of comic books owned by their creators rather than by publishers. The first book published by Image Comics was Liefeld's Youngblood #1."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dream_(character)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Dream of the Endless** is a [fictional](:Fiction) [anthropomorphic personification](:Anthropomorphic_personification) who first appeared in the first issue of *[The Sandman](:The_Sandman_%28comic_book%29)*, written by [Neil Gaiman](:Neil_Gaiman) and published by [DC Comics](:DC_Comics). One of the seven [Endless](:Endless_%28comics%29), who are inconceivably powerful beings older and greater than gods, Dream is both lord and personification of all [dreams](:Dream) and stories, all that is not in [reality](:Reality) (which, in turn, Dream may define by his existence). He has taken many names, including **[Morpheus](:Morpheus_%28mythology%29)** and **[Oneiros](:Oneiroi)**, and his appearance can change depending on the person who is seeing him. Dream was named the sixth-greatest comic book character by *[Empire Magazine](:Empire_Magazine)*. He was also named fifteenth in [IGN](:IGN)'s 100 Top Comic Book Heroes list.[Tom Sturridge](:Tom_Sturridge) portrays Dream in the television series *[The Sandman](:The_Sandman_%28TV_series%29)* on [Netflix](:Netflix), while Ernest Kingsley Jr. portrays him in the form of **[Kai'ckul](:Kai%27ckul)**."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
