<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Buster_Brown> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Buster Brown** is a [comic-strip](:Comic-strip) character created in 1902 by [Richard F. Outcault](:Richard_F%2E_Outcault). Adopted as the mascot of the [Brown Shoe Company](:Brown_Shoe_Company) in 1904, Buster Brown, along with Mary Jane, and with his dog Tige, became well known to the  [American](:United_States_of_America) public in the early-20th century. The character's name was used to describe a popular style of suit for young boys, the [Buster Brown suit](:Buster_Brown_suit), that reflected his outfit."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eagle_Awards> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q618779> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Supervision_(character)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Bridget Flynn** is a [fictional](:Fictional) [comic book](:Comic_book) [superheroine](:Superheroine), a member of the superhero team [Dynamo 5](:Dynamo_5), which appears in the monthly series of the same name from [Image Comics](:Image_Comics). Created by writer [Jay Faerber](:Jay_Faerber) and artist [Mahmud A. Asrar](:Mahmud_A%2E_Asrar), the character first appeared in *Dynamo 5* #1 (January 2007).For the first 24 issues of the series, the character possessed [superhuman strength](:Superhuman_strength) and invulnerability, and went by the codename **Scrap**. In issue #25 of the series (October 2009), the character, whose powers had been erased in the previous issue, obtained different powers. Now possessing laser, telescopic and x-ray vision, she goes by the codename **Supervision**."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
