<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Element_Girl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Element Girl** is a [superheroine](:Superheroine) appearing in [American comic books](:American_comic_book) published by [DC Comics](:DC_Comics). The character first appeared in *[Metamorpho](:Metamorpho)* #10 (February 1967), written by [Bob Haney](:Bob_Haney) and drawn by [Sal Trapani](:Sal_Trapani). Element Girl's death was featured in [Neil Gaiman](:Neil_Gaiman)'s *[Sandman](:Sandman_%28Vertigo%29)* series in issue #20, \"[Façade](:The_Sandman%3A_Dream_Country%23Fa%C3%A7ade)\". A similar character named **Element Woman** appeared during the events of [Flashpoint](:Flashpoint_%28comics%29) and later appearing in [The New 52](:The_New_52) as part of the Justice League. Both characters are similar in design to Metamorpho and have the same powers."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Manoj_Gupta> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/wikiPageRevisionID> "1118230452"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Supervision_(character)> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#resource_identifier> "0,97703"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Carmine_Infantino> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Carmine Michael Infantino** (; May 24, 1925 – April 4, 2013) was an American [comics artist](:Comics_artist) and [editor](:Editing), primarily for [DC Comics](:DC_Comics), during the late 1950s and early 1960s period known as the [Silver Age of Comic Books](:Silver_Age_of_Comic_Books). Among his character creations are the [Black Canary](:Black_Canary) and the [Silver Age version](:Flash_%28Barry_Allen%29) of DC superhero the [Flash](:Flash_%28DC_Comics_character%29) with writer [Robert Kanigher](:Robert_Kanigher), the stretching [Elongated Man](:Elongated_Man) with [John Broome](:John_Broome_%28writer%29), [Barbara Gordon](:Barbara_Gordon) the second [Batgirl](:Batgirl) with writer [Gardner Fox](:Gardner_Fox), [Deadman](:Deadman_%28comics%29) with writer [Arnold Drake](:Arnold_Drake), and Christopher Chance, the second iteration of the [Human Target](:Human_Target) with [Len Wein](:Len_Wein).He was inducted into comics' [Will Eisner Award Hall of Fame](:List_of_Eisner_Award_winners%23The_Will_Eisner_Award_Hall_of_Fame) in 2000."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
