<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Jim_Corrigan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Jim Corrigan** is the name of three fictional characters that have appeared in numerous comic books published by [DC Comics](:DC_Comics).The first Corrigan initially appeared in *[More Fun Comics](:More_Fun_Comics)* #52 (February 1940), a deceased cop acting as host to the cosmic entity the [Spectre](:Spectre_%28DC_Comics_character%29), and was created by [Jerry Siegel](:Jerry_Siegel) and [Bernard Baily](:Bernard_Baily).The second Jim Corrigan was an African-American policeman who has no relation with the original character, first appeared in *[Superman's Pal Jimmy Olsen](:Superman%27s_Pal_Jimmy_Olsen)* #149 (May 1972). The character was created by John Albano and [José Delbo](:Jos%C3%A9_Delbo). He later became a regular supporting character in *[Black Lightning](:Black_Lightning)* beginning with #4.The third Jim Corrigan appeared years later in issue #12 of *[Gotham Central](:Gotham_Central)*, a series about the [Gotham City Police Department](:Gotham_City_Police_Department). The character, created by [Greg Rucka](:Greg_Rucka), [Ed Brubaker](:Ed_Brubaker), and [Michael Lark](:Michael_Lark) although similar to the first Corrigan in being a police detective, again is not related to him and served as a red herring of who would become the new Spectre. This Corrigan is later revealed to be a corrupt, self-serving malefactor who murders his colleague Crispus Allen; Allen then becomes the host to the Spectre.Jim Corrigan appeared in a [live-action](:Live_action) portrayal by [Emmett J. Scanlan](:Emmett_J%2E_Scanlan) in the television series *[Constantine](:Constantine_%28TV_series%29)*. [Stephen Lobo](:Stephen_Lobo) also portrayed the character in the [Arrowverse](:Arrowverse) crossover *[Crisis on Infinite Earths](:Crisis_on_Infinite_Earths_%28Arrowverse%29)*."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
