<http://dbpedia.org/resource/The_Amazing_Screw-On_Head> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***The Amazing Screw-On Head*** is a [one-shot](:One-shot_%28comics%29) [comic book](:Comic_book) written and drawn by [Mike Mignola](:Mike_Mignola) and published by [Dark Horse Comics](:Dark_Horse_Comics) in [2002](:2002_in_comics), starring the character of the same name. *The Amazing Screw-On Head* stars a robot living during the [Lincoln administration](:Lincoln_administration) whose head can be attached to different bodies with different tactical abilities, and who functions as an agent of the U.S. government.The idea for the character was inspired by [action figures](:Action_figures), particularly [Batman](:Batman) ones, which seemed to Mignola to be the same figurines with different paint jobs. Mignola imagined a [robot](:Robot) with a head that screwed onto different bodies to suit the occasion, hence \"Screw-on Head\". An animated [pilot](:Television_pilot), based on the plot of the comic, was produced by the [Sci-Fi Channel](:Sci_Fi_Channel_%28United_States%29) in 2006, with [Bryan Fuller](:Bryan_Fuller) as writer and executive producer and [Chris Prynoski](:Chris_Prynoski) as director."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/E._Nelson_Bridwell> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#NaturalPerson> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dick_Sprang> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/wikiPageRevisionID> "1117421545"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Winky,_Blinky,_and_Noddy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Winky, Blinky, and Noddy** are a trio of fictional comic book characters, created by writer [Gardner Fox](:Gardner_Fox) and artist E.E. Hibbard, who first appeared in books starring [the Flash](:Flash_%28Jay_Garrick%29).Their names were taken from [Wynken, Blynken, and Nod](:Wynken%2C_Blynken%2C_and_Nod), although their appearance and characterization was a spoof on [the Three Stooges](:The_Three_Stooges). Noddy Moylan was based on [Moe Howard](:Moe_Howard), and often gave the other two a Stooges-style smack. Winky Boylan's red curly hair imitated [Larry Fine](:Larry_Fine)'s. Blinky Toylan's eyes were covered with a shock of hair, recalling [Shemp Howard](:Shemp_Howard). The comic books frequently referred to them as the \"Three Dimwits\", or variants like the \"Three Numbskulls\", the \"Three Dopes\", or the \"Three Idiots\"."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
