<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Grant_Morrison> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Grant Morrison**, [MBE](:Order_of_the_British_Empire) (born 31 January 1960) is a Scottish [comic book writer](:Comic_book_writer), [screenwriter](:Screenwriter), and producer. Their work is known for its [nonlinear](:Nonlinear_%28arts%29) [narratives](:Narrative), [humanist](:Humanist) philosophy and [countercultural](:Counterculture) leanings. Morrison has written extensively for the American comic book publisher [DC Comics](:DC_Comics), penning lengthy runs on *[Animal Man](:Animal_Man_%28comic_book%29)*, *[Doom Patrol](:Doom_Patrol)*, *[JLA](:JLA_%28comic_book%29)*, *[Action Comics](:Action_Comics)*, and *[The Green Lantern](:The_Green_Lantern)* as well as the graphic novels *[Arkham Asylum](:Arkham_Asylum%3A_A_Serious_House_on_Serious_Earth)* and *[Wonder Woman: Earth One](:Wonder_Woman%3A_Earth_One)*, the meta-series *[Seven Soldiers](:Seven_Soldiers)* and *[The Multiversity](:The_Multiversity)*, the mini-series *[DC One Million](:DC_One_Million)* and *[Final Crisis](:Final_Crisis)*, both of which served as centrepieces for the eponymous company-wide crossover storylines, and the maxi-series *[All-Star Superman](:All-Star_Superman)*. Morrison's best known DC work is the seven-year [Batman](:Batman) storyline which started in the *[Batman](:Batman_%28comic_book%29)* ongoing series and continued through *Final Crisis*, *[Batman and Robin](:Batman_and_Robin_%28comic_book%29)*, *[Batman: The Return of Bruce Wayne](:Batman%3A_The_Return_of_Bruce_Wayne)* and two volumes of *[Batman Incorporated](:Batman_Incorporated)*.Morrison's creator-owned work, the bulk of which was published through DC Comics' [Vertigo](:Vertigo_%28DC_Comics%29) imprint, includes *[Flex Mentallo](:Flex_Mentallo)* and *[We3](:We3)* with Scottish artist [Frank Quitely](:Frank_Quitely), *[Seaguy](:Seaguy)* with artist [Cameron Stewart](:Cameron_Stewart), *[The Filth](:The_Filth_%28comics%29)* with [Chris Weston](:Chris_Weston), and the three-volume series *[The Invisibles](:The_Invisibles)*. At [Marvel](:Marvel_Comics), Morrison wrote a three-year run on *[New X-Men](:New_X-Men_%282001_series%29)* and created *[Marvel Boy](:Noh-Varr)* for the publisher's [Marvel Knights](:Marvel_Knights) imprint.Between 2016 and 2018, Morrison served as the Editor-in-Chief of the *[Heavy Metal](:Heavy_Metal_%28magazine%29)* magazine.Morrison's work has drawn critical acclaim. They have won numerous awards, including [Eisner](:Eisner_Award), [Harvey](:Harvey_Awards), and [Inkpot](:Inkpot_Award) awards. In 2012, Morrison was appointed [Member of the Order of the British Empire](:Member_of_the_Order_of_the_British_Empire) (MBE) for services to film and literature."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
