<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dave_Cockrum> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**David Emmett Cockrum** (; November 11, 1943 – November 26, 2006) was an American [comics artist](:Comics_artist) known for his co-creation of the new [X-Men](:X-Men) characters [Nightcrawler](:Nightcrawler_%28comics%29), [Storm](:Storm_%28Marvel_Comics%29), [Colossus](:Colossus_%28comics%29), and [Mystique](:Mystique_%28character%29), as well as the antiheroine [Black Cat](:Black_Cat_%28Marvel_Comics%29). Cockrum was a prolific and inventive costume designer who updated the uniforms of the [Legion of Super-Heroes](:Legion_of_Super-Heroes). He did the same for the new X-Men and many of their antagonists in the 1970s and early 1980s."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Corvus_Glaive> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/givenName> "Corvus Glaive"@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Howard_Mackie> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Howard Mackie** (born January 22, 1958) is an American comic book editor and writer. He has worked almost exclusively for [Marvel Comics](:Marvel_Comics) and is best known as the co-creator of the [Danny Ketch](:Ghost_Rider_%28Danny_Ketch%29) version of the [Ghost Rider](:Ghost_Rider) character."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Proteus_(Marvel_Comics)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Kevin MacTaggert, best known as Proteus and also called Mutant X, is a character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. The character is commonly associated with the X-Men. Kevin was the mutant son of Scottish genetic researcher Moira MacTaggert and politician Joseph MacTaggert. Kevin had reality-warping and possession powers and lived most of his life in forced seclusion at his mother's Muir Island research facility."@en .
