<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Storm_(Marvel_Comics)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Storm** is a [superhero](:Superhero) appearing in [American comic books](:American_comic_books) published by [Marvel Comics](:Marvel_Comics). The character was created by writer [Len Wein](:Len_Wein) and artist [Dave Cockrum](:Dave_Cockrum), first appearing in *[Giant-Size X-Men](:Giant-Size_X-Men)* #1 (May 1975). Descended from a long line of African witch-priestesses, Storm is a member of a fictional subspecies of humans born with [superhuman abilities](:Superpower_%28ability%29) known as [mutants](:Mutant_%28Marvel_Comics%29). She is able to control the weather and atmosphere and is considered to be one of the most powerful mutants on the planet, and one of the most powerful beings in the [Marvel Universe](:Marvel_Universe).Born **Ororo Munroe** to a tribal princess of [Kenya](:Kenya) and an African-American photojournalist father, Storm is raised in [Harlem](:Harlem), New York City, United States and [Cairo](:Cairo), Egypt. She was made an orphan after her parents were killed in the midst of an [Arab–Israeli conflict](:Arab%E2%80%93Israeli_conflict). An incident at this time also traumatized Munroe, leaving her with [claustrophobia](:Claustrophobia) that she would struggle with for life. Storm is a member of the [X-Men](:X-Men), a group of mutant heroes fighting for peace and equal rights between mutants and humans. Under the tutelage of a master thief an adolescent Munroe became a skilled [pickpocket](:Pickpocketing), the means of which she meets through coincidence the powerful mutant [Professor X](:Professor_X). Professor X later convinces Munroe to join the X-Men and use her abilities for a greater cause and purpose. Possessing natural leadership skills and formidable powers of her own, Storm has led the X-Men at times and has been a member of teams such as the [Avengers](:Avengers_%28comics%29) and the [Fantastic Four](:Fantastic_Four) as well. Storm is also part of one of the higher-profile romantic relationships in all of comics. Having married childhood sweetheart and fellow superhero [Black Panther](:Black_Panther_%28comics%29), the ruler of the fictional African nation of [Wakanda](:Wakanda), Munroe was made [queen consort](:Queen_consort) through marriage. The title was lost however when the two later divorced.Created during the [Bronze Age of Comic Books](:Bronze_Age_of_Comic_Books), Storm is the first major female character of African descent in comics. She is regarded by some as being Marvel Comics' most important female superhero, having drawn favorable comparison to [DC Comics](:DC_Comics)' most famous female lead [Wonder Woman](:Wonder_Woman). When Marvel and DC Comics published a *[DC vs. Marvel](:DC_vs%2E_Marvel)* miniseries in 1996, Storm was pitted against Wonder Woman in a one-on-one battle and emerged victorious due to winning a popular vote amongst readers.Storm has been described as one of Marvel's most notable and powerful female heroes.One of the most prominent characters in the X-Men series, Storm has appeared in various forms of media relating to the franchise, including animation, television, video games, and a series of films.The character was first portrayed in live-action by [Halle Berry](:Halle_Berry) in 2000 film *[X-Men](:X-Men_%28film%29)*. Berry returned to portray the role in the films *[X2](:X2_%28film%29),* *[X-Men: The Last Stand](:X-Men%3A_The_Last_Stand),* and *[X-Men: Days of Future Past](:X-Men%3A_Days_of_Future_Past).* The younger version of Storm was portrayed by [Alexandra Shipp](:Alexandra_Shipp) in the 2016 film *[X-Men: Apocalypse](:X-Men%3A_Apocalypse)*. Shipp had a cameo in *[Deadpool 2](:Deadpool_2)* and reprised her role in the 2019 film *[X-Men: Dark Phoenix](:X-Men%3A_Dark_Phoenix)*."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Batman_of_Zur-En-Arrh> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Batman of Zur-En-Arrh** is a [fictional character](:Fictional_character) in the [DC Comics universe](:DC_Comics_universe). In the [Silver Age](:Silver_Age_of_Comic_Books) story, the character is an alien named **Tlano** from the planet Zur-En-Arrh who decided to become a version of Batman for his own planet. The character's reappearance in the 2000s rebranded him as a violent and unhinged [backup personality](:Dissociative_identity_disorder) of [Bruce Wayne](:Batman)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
