<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Gardner_Fox> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Gardner Francis Cooper Fox** (May 20, 1911 – [December 24](:Christmas_Eve), 1986) was an American writer known best for creating numerous comic book characters for [DC Comics](:DC_Comics). He is estimated to have written more than 4,000 comics stories, including 1,500 for [DC Comics](:DC_Comics). Fox was also a science fiction author and wrote many novels and short stories.Fox is known as the co-creator of DC Comics heroes [Barbara Gordon](:Barbara_Gordon), the original [Flash](:Flash_%28Jay_Garrick%29), [Hawkman](:Hawkman_%28Carter_Hall%29), [Doctor Fate](:Doctor_Fate), [Zatanna](:Zatanna) and the original [Sandman](:Sandman_%28Wesley_Dodds%29), and was the writer who first teamed several of those and other heroes as the [Justice Society of America](:Justice_Society_of_America), and later recreated the team as the [Justice League of America](:Justice_League). Fox introduced the concept of the [Multiverse](:Multiverse_%28DC_Comics%29) to DC Comics in the 1961 story \"[Flash of Two Worlds](:Flash_of_Two_Worlds)!\""^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
