<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dan_DeCarlo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Daniel S. DeCarlo** (December 12, 1919 – December 18, 2001) was an American [cartoonist](:Cartoonist) best known for having developed the look of [Archie Comics](:Archie_Comics) in the late 1950s and early 1960s, modernizing the characters to their contemporary appearance and establishing the publisher's house style up until his death. As well, he is the generally recognized co-creator of the characters [Sabrina the Teenage Witch](:Sabrina_the_Teenage_Witch), [Josie and the Pussycats](:Josie_and_the_Pussycats_%28comics%29) (the title character of which was named for his wife), and [Cheryl Blossom](:Cheryl_Blossom)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Don_Heck> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Donald L. Heck (January 2, 1929 – February 23, 1995) was an American comics artist best known for co-creating the Marvel Comics characters Iron Man, the Wasp, Black Widow, Hawkeye and Wonder Man and for his long run penciling the Marvel superhero-team series The Avengers during the 1960s Silver Age of comic books."@en .
